{% comment %}
  Standalone Section Rendering API data endpoint for the `product-finder` block.

  Fetched (never placed) via `sectionRenderer.getSectionHTML('section-rendering-product-finder', false, url)`
  where `url` is the target collection URL carrying cumulative `filter.*` params. Because the request URL
  is the collection URL, `collection` resolves to that collection and `?filter.*` is honored — so
  `collection.filters` comes back narrowed in true collection context (Shopify recomputes each filter's
  value counts against the active selection).

  Dumps EVERY filter as a bare `<select data-filter-name data-filter-label>` of its `count > 0` values.
  The finder JS reads the ones it maps to. Renders nothing useful when viewed directly (no collection) —
  that is expected; it is an API-only endpoint.
{% endcomment %}

<div hidden>
  {%- for filter in collection.filters -%}
    <select data-filter-name="{{ filter.param_name }}" data-filter-label="{{ filter.label | escape }}">
      {%- for value in filter.values -%}
        {%- if value.count > 0 -%}
          <option value="{{ value.value | escape }}" data-count="{{ value.count }}">{{ value.label }}</option>
        {%- endif -%}
      {%- endfor -%}
    </select>
  {%- endfor -%}
</div>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "t:names.product_finder_rendering",
  "disabled_on": {
    "groups": ["header", "footer"]
  },
  "settings": []
}
{% endschema %}
